# amont-agent-cases-v1
# Reviewed judgements for this rule. Generated by
#   amont-agent explain <rule> --format cases
# then labelled by hand. `amont-agent corpus check` replays every line through
# the rules as they stand today, and runs as a test — so widening a rule in a
# way that breaks a judgement somebody already made is a red build.
#
# match   the rule SHOULD fire here
# nomatch the rule must stay silent here — these are the ones that matter,
#         because a corpus of positives alone measures recall, not precision
# ?       nobody has looked yet; never counts as evidence
#
# This rule is advise-only (max stance advise). `examine` judges the name of
# the path and the program that reads it; `confirm` (the file exists, a key
# file holds a PRIVATE KEY) is not run by the corpus, so no case here depends
# on a file's content. A `Read <window> <bytes> <agent> <path>` line is a Read
# call, judged by the same name test the hook makes (`secret_read::judge_case`).
# Hand-written from the plan's examples (2026-11-20), not mined: the rule is new.

# --- the rule should fire ---
match	cat ~/.netrc
match	cat ~/.netrc | pbcopy
match	grep token ~/.aws/credentials
match	cp ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 /tmp/k
match	head -3 .env
match	cat "$HOME/.netrc"
match	cat ${HOME}/.docker/config.json
match	jq . < .env
match	cat < ~/.netrc
match	grep -e ghp_ ~/.netrc
match	tail -n 5 ~/.claude/.credentials.json
match	cat ~/.ssh/id_*
match	Read full 120 main ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
match	Read 1:50 400 general-purpose /Users/x/.aws/credentials
match	Read full 90 main app/.env

# --- the rule must stay silent ---
# A credential used by reference, not read.
nomatch	curl -n https://x
nomatch	curl --cert ~/.config/mtls/c.crt --key ~/.config/mtls/c.key https://x
nomatch	ls ~/.ssh
nomatch	ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
# Public halves and templates.
nomatch	cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
nomatch	cat ~/.ssh/known_hosts
nomatch	cat .env.example
nomatch	Read full 90 main app/.env.sample
# A quiet form shows no bytes.
nomatch	grep -q x ~/.netrc
nomatch	grep -qi x ~/.netrc
nomatch	rg -l token ~/.aws/credentials
# The first operand of a pattern reader is the pattern, not a path.
nomatch	grep .env README.md
# A write, a copy toward a secret, and output that goes to the shell.
nomatch	sed -i 's/a/b/' .env
nomatch	cp /tmp/k ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
nomatch	X=$(cat ~/.netrc)
# Configuration, not a secret.
nomatch	cat ~/.claude/settings.json
nomatch	Read full 3000 main ~/.claude/settings.json
